{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/test-plugin.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-09-29T14:06:52.354302Z","id":"ea58f4e6a16853c6be914b11009ea4e685019293cb6b1343041e1574686159db","body":{"detail":"scripts/test-plugin.sh:414-423 does `case \"$(uname -s)-$(uname -m)\"` once and sets TARGET/SHAVAR for that single platform only (falling back to 'skip: no release target ... download tests skipped' for anything else); every D-series test after that (D1-D10) runs exclusively against that one target. ensure-qualifier.sh's resolve_target() (161-168) and expected_sha256() (170-176) are two independently-maintained case statements that must stay in exact lockstep across three targets (aarch64-apple-darwin, x86_64-unknown-linux-musl, aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu) plus the three SHA256_* variables (53-55). Since CI presumably runs on one OS/arch, a mismatch introduced for either of the other two targets (e.g. a copy-paste error swapping two SHA256_* values, or a target string that resolve_target() emits but expected_sha256() doesn't recognize) would pass this test suite and only surface when a user on that platform actually tries to install, hitting a checksum-mismatch or cargo-fallback error at session start.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":414},"end":{"line":423},"content_hash":"8208ea3f95fb81c2352261e197d9eb1725ca7aad3018ca9275f512933a4a5288"},"suggested_fix":"Parameterize the D-series download tests (or at least a lighter subset: D2/D8/D9) over all three known targets by building fixture releases and pinned wrapper copies per target rather than only `$(uname -s)-$(uname -m)`, so a wiring mistake in an untested-locally platform is still caught in CI.","summary":"The download/checksum tests exercise only the single release target matching the CI runner's own OS/arch, leaving the other two resolve_target()/expected_sha256() platform mappings in ensure-qualifier.sh completely untested","tags":["review","review:claude-plugin-pr14","session:claude-code:6982e520-2dd9-4d9d-b484-c954e628c65c"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/test-plugin.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-09-29T14:17:14.840061Z","id":"5b5227d7e288f1f87fc815f1b7b966672131f0b51e49dc31ef7bfa15ce652508","body":{"detail":"scripts/test-plugin.sh:414-423 selects one TARGET/SHAVAR from $(uname -s)-$(uname -m) and skips the download tests on any other host. This mapping is a third copy, kept separately from resolve_target() and expected_sha256() in plugins/claude-code/scripts/ensure-qualifier.sh:161-176. .github/workflows/ci.yml:27 runs scripts/test-plugin.sh, and both jobs in that file run on ubuntu-latest (:14, :24), so CI exercises only x86_64-unknown-linux-musl. No other file in scripts/ or .github/ references SHA256_*, expected_sha256, or resolve_target. The aarch64-apple-darwin and aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu mappings and checksums are therefore never checked in CI.","kind":"comment","references":"ea58f4e6a16853c6be914b11009ea4e685019293cb6b1343041e1574686159db","summary":"confirmed: the download and checksum tests cover only the host's target, and CI runs only on ubuntu-latest","tags":["verified","session:claude-code:6982e520-2dd9-4d9d-b484-c954e628c65c"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/test-plugin.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T17:00:14.408668Z","id":"c7bd4ee92d5f08cbb8d701bc6b4bfddb15c766f9f2e8e7a0692f8b51a6ce52b6","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f475034bf27aef3af52166a50ed08a4a7f10904f","summary":"the download/checksum tests now loop over all three release targets (aarch64-apple-darwin, x86_64-unknown-linux-musl, aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu), not just the host's: scripts/test-plugin.sh ok: every platform mapping resolves to its target (also via prebuilt-target) with a 64-hex-digit embedded checksum; ok: downloads, verifies, and installs the release for every target; CI also now runs the suite under macOS's system bash (.github/workflows/ci.yml matrix: macos-latest, bash=/bin/bash), via commit 158d727abc5a5503af9c79d48a178300af866b54","supersedes":"ea58f4e6a16853c6be914b11009ea4e685019293cb6b1343041e1574686159db","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6982e520-2dd9-4d9d-b484-c954e628c65c"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/check-skill-examples.py","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:16:51.817428Z","id":"035806347f0e992a157d81b98099a9015acc84b74670b0760d89894d123a1bc9","body":{"detail":"check-skill-examples.py:480-497 uses $QUALIFIER_BIN, else target/debug or target/release. .github/workflows/ci.yml:39 sets QUALIFIER_BIN to the checkout's target/debug/qualifier. The plugin, though, only runs the release named by PINNED_VERSION (ensure-qualifier.sh:65), and marketplace.json:17 serves the plugin from ./plugins/claude-code on the default branch. AGENTS.md (Keeping Things in Sync) requires skills to change in the same commit as a CLI rename, and also requires PINNED_VERSION to move only in a later plugin release. Together those mean main can carry skills that use a new flag while the pinned binary is still the old release. CI stays green because it checks the new build, and users who install from main get skills their binary rejects. scripts/eval-plugin.sh:46-48 has the same split: scaffold fixtures use the checkout build on PATH, while the model's sessions go through the wrapper, which never consults PATH and so runs the pinned release. Nothing compares PINNED_VERSION with Cargo.toml's version. Today both are 0.8.0, so there is no live failure.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":480},"end":{"line":497},"content_hash":"c0c364893716ee89174e4c0fcf58f22500eee5aa57ec88abdac1757407858f7d"},"suggested_fix":"In scripts/test-plugin.sh, fail when the skill-example binary's `--version` differs from `qualifier $PINNED` unless the run explicitly opts in (for example ALLOW_UNPINNED_SKILLS=1 for development). Or add a CI step that downloads the pinned release tarball, verifies it against the embedded SHA256_* value, and runs check-skill-examples.py against it as well. Say in AGENTS.md which binary the skills on main must work with.","summary":"The skill examples run against the working-tree build, but the shipped plugin runs PINNED_VERSION, so CI can pass on skills the pinned binary rejects","tags":["review","review:2026-10-01","session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/test-plugin.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:16:51.817535Z","id":"0c2a993cebf7cbc0ce8a6d46d5b4b0d7a4178b43d74e6f0e61f8b647492a57c3","body":{"detail":"AGENTS.md (Keeping Things in Sync, plugins/claude-code/ bullet) says to \"bump the plugin version for any skill, hook, or wrapper change\". The manifest check at test-plugin.sh:53-70 only checks that marketplace.json and plugin.json agree. https://code.claude.com/docs/en/plugins-reference#version says that setting `version` \"pins the plugin to that version until you change it\". A merged skill or hook change that doesn't bump plugins/claude-code/.claude-plugin/plugin.json (now 0.1.0) never reaches installed users. Nothing in CI catches it, because the versions still agree.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":53},"end":{"line":70},"content_hash":"6989922e99568acca1efd1165e18319128aa3858cd8645de849be7c76e618b79"},"suggested_fix":"In CI on pull requests, compare against the merge base: if any file under plugins/claude-code/ other than evals/ and .qual files changed, and plugin.json's version did not, fail with a message that names the rule.","summary":"Nothing enforces the plugin version bump that AGENTS.md requires for any skill, hook, or wrapper change, so users can stay on stale skills","tags":["review","review:2026-10-01","session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/check-skill-examples.py","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:18:41.780148Z","id":"0bd7333d47d2bdd322ce1723af028cbc3060b8521f73f77bab013b0a59d84fae","body":{"detail":"scripts/check-skill-examples.py:480-497 picks $QUALIFIER_BIN or target/{debug,release}/qualifier. .github/workflows/ci.yml sets QUALIFIER_BIN to ${{ github.workspace }}/target/debug/qualifier after `cargo build`. check-skill-examples.py:512 reads `--version` but only prints it (line 615), never compares it. plugins/claude-code/scripts/ensure-qualifier.sh:65 has PINNED_VERSION=\"0.8.0\", and scripts/test-plugin.sh:216 hardcodes 0.8.0 without reading Cargo.toml. Cargo.toml:3 is 0.8.0 today, so nothing fails yet. Concern is the right kind.","kind":"comment","references":"035806347f0e992a157d81b98099a9015acc84b74670b0760d89894d123a1bc9","summary":"confirmed: skill examples run against the checkout build, and nothing ties that build to PINNED_VERSION","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/test-plugin.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:18:41.780163Z","id":"a8a8cbe929323b3c2113ef66878179922015dc4a18e58d59397b1f9241b91adc","body":{"detail":"scripts/test-plugin.sh:53-70 asserts the name, the source, and `entry[\"version\"] == plugin[\"version\"]`. No check compares against the merge base. plugins/claude-code/.claude-plugin/plugin.json:3 is \"0.1.0\". https://code.claude.com/docs/en/plugins-reference#version says: \"Setting it pins the plugin to that version until you change it\".","kind":"comment","references":"0c2a993cebf7cbc0ce8a6d46d5b4b0d7a4178b43d74e6f0e61f8b647492a57c3","summary":"confirmed: CI checks only that the two manifest versions agree, not that the version was bumped","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/test-plugin.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:33:23.212704Z","id":"7183f6e6ae3bd0b19be3ce3022f3db18f6032c8e3eb58681fc0e082cb6603208","body":{"detail":"Evidence: scripts/test-plugin.sh:53-70 asserts only entry[\"version\"] == plugin[\"version\"]; https://code.claude.com/docs/en/plugins-reference#version","kind":"comment","references":"0c2a993cebf7cbc0ce8a6d46d5b4b0d7a4178b43d74e6f0e61f8b647492a57c3","summary":"Resolution: Add a pull-request CI step in .github/workflows/ci.yml (or a mode of scripts/test-plugin.sh) that diffs against the merge base: if any file under plugins/claude-code/ outside evals/ and .qual changed and .claude-plugin/plugin.json's version did not, fail with a message that cites the AGENTS.md rule.","tags":["session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/check-skill-examples.py","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:34:02.796894Z","id":"985930b08fc9f5f1c15e7bbc5a7015e348f8f718df09c39838b7b5639508c0e7","body":{"detail":"Option A: the pinned release; CI downloads it, checks SHA256_*, and runs check-skill-examples.py on it; skill edits for a CLI rename then wait for the plugin release, which changes the AGENTS.md same-commit rule. Option B: the checkout build; test-plugin.sh fails when --version differs from PINNED_VERSION unless ALLOW_UNPINNED_SKILLS=1. Record the choice in AGENTS.md. Recommendation: B; it keeps the existing same-commit rule and still catches skills drifting from the pinned release.","kind":"comment","references":"035806347f0e992a157d81b98099a9015acc84b74670b0760d89894d123a1bc9","summary":"Needs a decision: Which binary must the skills on main work with: the pinned release or the checkout build?","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/check-skill-examples.py","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"human","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:43:48.528807Z","id":"4e49ec66d3a9d5b8676d839ffff05ac710c15a43119851cac321964e5db4c89d","body":{"detail":"The checkout build, with a version check","kind":"comment","references":"035806347f0e992a157d81b98099a9015acc84b74670b0760d89894d123a1bc9","summary":"Decided: skills on main are checked against the checkout build, with a version check. scripts/test-plugin.sh fails when the built qualifier --version differs from PINNED_VERSION unless ALLOW_UNPINNED_SKILLS=1 is set; record the rule in AGENTS.md. The same-commit rule for skill edits stays.","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
